    "Your questions cover %@ of the notes you've added." : {},
    "Your questions cover %@ of your material." : {},
    "Your questions join this exam as you add notes." : {},
    "Your questions to Cap, and with each one the notes of the course Cap is answering from (every course, if you chose All courses): the text of your pages and lectures, the cards of decks you imported and the names of what you added. All of it when it's short, otherwise the parts that fit your question. When you ask Cap to look through your notes, the passages it finds in any of your courses go too. If you snap a problem, only its words go, never the photo. So Cap can make things for the right course, it also sees the names of your courses, topics and exams, your exam dates, how ready you are, which topics are fading and how many questions are due. If you ask it to research something online, that topic is searched on trusted study sites." : {},
